00:47:27,272 --> 00:47:33,272
Twins of Evil (also known as Twins of Dracula) is a 1971 British horror film directed by John Hough and starring Peter Cushing, with Damien Thomas,
real-life identical twins: former Playboy Playmates Madeleine and Mary Collinson, Isobel Black, Kathleen Byron, Damien Thomas and David Warbeck.

13
00:51:24,545 --> 00:51:30,545
This was the Collinson sisters' final acting roles.

14
00:55:21,818 --> 00:55:27,818
It is the third (and final) film in the Karnstein Trilogy, based
on the 1872 novella Carmilla by Sheridan Le Fanu.

15
00:59:19,090 --> 00:59:25,090
The film has the least resemblance to the novella and adds
a witchfinding theme to the vampire story.

16
01:03:16,363 --> 01:03:22,363
Much of the interest of the film revolves around the contrasting evil and
good natures of two beautiful sisters, Frieda and Maria.

17
01:07:13,636 --> 01:07:19,636
Unlike the previous two entries in the series, this film
contains only a brief lesbian element.

18
